    "safety": {
      "level": "high-risk",
      "text": "The UK advises against all travel to the whole of Mali. It says JNIM has implemented blockades on key routes in southern and western Mali, including around Bamako, targeting fuel trucks and enforcing checkpoints for travellers, that leaving by overland routes to neighbouring countries is too dangerous, and that there is a high threat of kidnapping across Mali, including in Bamako. Canada says Mali has been ruled by a military-led transitional government since the August 2020 coup.",
      "source": {
        "url": "https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mali",
        "name": "UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office — Mali travel advice",
        "type": "government",
        "lastVerified": "2026-10-03",
